# Shell scripts must be LF: CRLF breaks the shebang and gives `$'\r'` errors
# under Git Bash / WSL / CI. The git hooks are shell scripts too, and a hook
# that fails to start is a guard that protects nothing.
*.sh text eol=lf
.githooks/* text eol=lf

# C# / MSBuild sources are edited in Visual Studio on Windows — keep them CRLF
# in the working tree so a build or an IDE save does not rewrite every line.
*.cs text eol=crlf
*.csproj text eol=crlf
*.manifest text eol=crlf

# PowerShell must be CRLF *and* keep its BOM (see CLAUDE.md): PS 5.1 reads a
# BOM-less file as CP1251 and mangles non-ASCII.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# CMD batch files must be CRLF — with LF ends cmd.exe misparses multi-line
# `( )` blocks and goto loops. Kept LAST: in .gitattributes the last matching
# rule wins.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf

# Binary: never normalize.
*.ico binary
